<title>USA: US weekly soybean crush 23,014,000 bushels -- NOPA.</title>
<headline>US weekly soybean crush 23,014,000 bushels -- NOPA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 07/09/97    07/02/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 23,014,000  24,386,000    26,570,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  68,083	95,056	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,451,000  35,451,000    34,100,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,643,944  35,643,944	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   07/09/97    07/02/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   3,797,000   4,338,000     4,598,000</p>
<p> Ind,Ky,Ohio,Mich 4,277,000   4,276,000     4,537,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,526,000   4,010,000     4,185,000</p>
<p> South Central    1,677,000   1,865,000     2,879,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,312,000   3,363,000     3,490,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,603,000   4,638,000     4,967,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,822,000   1,895,000     1,914,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	23,014,000  24,386,000    26,570,000</p>
</text>
